==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|tǫnn}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*tanþs}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₃dónts}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tʰœnː/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|œnː|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|tannar|tennur}}

# a [[tooth]]

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-f-s3|t|a|nn}}
There also exist the variant plural forms ''tannir'' and ''tönnur'', but these forms are neither original nor considered standard today, and have now become obsolete.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|falskar tennur}} (dentures)
* {{l|is|framtönn}} (incisor)
* {{l|is|höggriftönn}} (impact ripper)
* {{l|is|jaðartönn}} (corner tooth)
* {{l|is|mögnunartönn}} (exciter tooth)
* {{l|is|skaðlegur tönnum}} (cariogenic)
* {{l|is|taka tennur}} (to be teething, to cut teeth)

